{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Imagine you are asked to store the age of one student. That is a variable — give it a name, put a number in it, done. Now the request changes: store the age of every student in a lecture hall of 108."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Nothing you know so far breaks, exactly. You can still solve it. But watch what solving it actually costs."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Doing it the obvious way"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You would need 108 names, invented by hand, each holding one number:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "let age1 = 19;\nlet age2 = 21;\nlet age3 = 20;\n// ... 104 more lines ...\nlet age108 = 22;"
    },
